===============================================================================
LINKING EXCEPTION -- Plugin SDK boundary
===============================================================================

As a special exception to the terms of the AGPL-3.0 above, the following
does NOT constitute a "modified version" or "derivative work" of Portaless
under this license, and creating or distributing it under any license of
your choosing (including proprietary/closed-source licenses) is explicitly
permitted:

  1. Any plugin, extension, or module that runs isolated inside the
     Portaless plugin sandbox (packages/plugin-sandbox) and communicates
     with the Portaless core exclusively through the public Plugin SDK
     surface (the types, interfaces, and capability-bridge contracts
     published under packages/plugin-sdk, licensed separately under MIT --
     see LICENSE-SDK).

  2. Any software that merely uses the public HTTP APIs exposed by a
     running Portaless instance (e.g. the .well-known endpoints, the
     admin REST endpoints) without incorporating Portaless source code.

This exception does NOT cover:

  - Any code that directly imports, copies, patches, or statically/
    dynamically links against Portaless core source code outside of the
    published Plugin SDK surface.
  - Any modified version of the Portaless core itself (functions/,
    packages/ excluding plugin-sdk, src/) offered as a network service to
    third parties -- such modifications must be released under AGPL-3.0
    per Section 13 of the license above.

See docs/architecture/licensing-boundaries.md for the full explanation of
where this line is drawn, and for the separate licensing terms that apply
to the AppPlace and AppLibre plugin registries, which are independent
projects not covered by this LICENSE file.

The full legal text of the GNU Affero General Public License version 3 is
available at: https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.txt
